        "claim": "The search loop can infinite-loop when the first candidate on a valid day is after `limit`: `found` is set to True even when `candidate > limit`, so the code neither returns nor advances `current`, and the `while current <= limit` loop repeats forever. Example: `after=datetime(2024,1,1,10,0)`, `expr=\"0 11 * * *\"` should raise ValueError because the next fire is after 3000 days, but the code loops indefinitely.",
        "severity": "high",
        "status": "dropped",
        "investigation": "no deterministic repro; dropped (not repaired)"
      },
      {
        "id": "2",
        "file": "cron.py",
        "claim": "The 3000-day bound is not enforced correctly for candidates that fall after `limit` on the final eligible day; instead of advancing to the next day or raising, the code treats an out-of-limit candidate as a found candidate and stalls, violating the docstring requirement to raise ValueError when no match exists within 3000 days.",
        "severity": "high",
        "status": "dropped",
        "investigation": "no deterministic repro; dropped (not repaired)"
      },
      {
        "id": "3",
        "file": "cron.py",
        "claim": "When `current.month` is not in `month_set`, the code jumps to the first day of the next month at 00:00, which can skip the remainder of the current day if `current` is not already at 00:00. Although no match can occur in an invalid month, this jump also discards the current time context and can interact poorly with the limit boundary; a safer implementation should normalize to the next day or next month without assuming no later same-day state is needed.",
        "severity": "low",
        "status": "dropped",
